    "title": "Cold Weather Advisory issued through the morning - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Maia Mielke ,\n1 hours ago The National Weather Service in Binghamton, N.Y., and State College, Pa. have issued the following alerts: ‚ö†Ô∏èCOLD WEATHER ADVISORY: Very cold wind chills as low as 15 to 20 degrees below zero expected.\nüìçWHERE: Steuben County in New York, and Tioga County in Pennsylvania\n‚è∞WHEN: From 11 PM tonight until 9 AM Thursday in Steuben County. From 1 AM until 10 AM on Thursday, for Tioga County, PA.\n* IMPACTS... The cold wind chills as low as 20 below zero could\nresult in hypothermia or frostbite if precautions are not taken. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WETM - MyTwinTiers.com.",
